  "Number": 19,
  "Question": "If the length and width of a rectangle are each increased by \\(10\\%,\\) then the perimeter of the rectangle is increased by",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(10\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(21\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(40\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Perimeter adds side lengths, so the common increase factor can be factored out of the sum. Let the original length and width be \\(\\ell>0\\) and \\(w>0\\). The original perimeter is \\(P=2(\\ell+w)>0\\).\n\nA \\(10\\%\\) increase multiplies each dimension by \\(1.1\\), so the new perimeter is\n\\[\n2(1.1\\ell+1.1w)=1.1\\,[2(\\ell+w)]=1.1P.\n\\]\nThe increase is therefore \\(0.1P\\), which is \\(\\boxed{10\\%}\\) of the original perimeter, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
